                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game had an interesting premise and I did enjoy the references for popular MOBAS. I'd probably enjoy the minigames and dialogue options as well, but HOLY HELL, Echo Star is BAD. (That's the MOBA you'll need to play A LOT to progress through the story.)\n\nThe tutorial is incredibly long, dull and boring and at first, I thought they just fucked up designing the tutorial. But no. Big no. Echo Star itself is ALSO incredibly long, dull and boring. You cant design an enjoyable tutorial if the game itself isn't even enjoyable, right?\n\nAs I mentioned earlier, you'll need to invest a lot of time into Echo Star to progress. You cant skip it. You can play it on easy mode, but even then it takes pretty long to get through one match and honestly, I'm not willing to invest 30 minutes of my time into a match to get 5 minutes of dialogue and a mini game. \n\nIt's a shame because I was really looking forward to Elo Hell. Sadly, they fucked up the key feature of the game, making it unplayable to me.",
